      "writtenOn": "2022-09-21T14:24:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s unfortunate that a unit test like this interacts with the real DeviceConfig class.\n\nI know that both DeviceConfig and DeviceConfigUtils are used via static methods that can\u0027t be mocked, but this seems like a case for dependency injection or a wrapper class. IIRC in the past Remi and I had discussed a FlagManager class that would encapsulate flagging functionality (e.g., figure out the right namespace, get the apex module version, etc.) and unlike DeviceConfigUtils would be mockable. That would make sense to pass to CS via dependency injection and that could then pass it to MultinetworkPolicyTracker.\n\nThat\u0027s probably a bigger task than you want to do right now, but maybe add a TODO for it?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5810,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 5810,
        "endChar": 47
      },
      "revId": "cd3ccf709b1aabfc46c131b83b94b4110e142bd7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
